+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a flip take in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About six months from purchase to resale. The middle home resold within a year in Horry County sold again 191 days after its purchase, and the middle half took about four to ten months."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I flip a house in Myrtle Beach from out of state?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A Chapter3 agent walks the house on video, runs the numbers, and lines up the closing attorney and the inspector. Our page for out-of-state buyers explains how a closing works from a distance."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to use BrickWood Mortgage?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. You may use any lender you like. BrickWood Mortgage is our preferred lender for fix-and-flip and bridge loans."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you need a license to flip houses in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No real estate license is needed to buy and sell a house you own. The contractors you hire need theirs, and the permits section above shows which work needs a license."}}]}</script>
