-<div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/strategies/">Strategies</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Fix and Flip</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Strategy</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Fix and flip in Myrtle Beach:<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">the costs, and a house that sold the day work ended.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Chapter3 Realty &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated October 27, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">What a fix and flip costs on the Grand Strand, how the financing works, and one real example that sold the day construction ended.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The strategy</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 1.2rem;line-height:1.1">Fix and flip math for Myrtle Beach.</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px">A fix and flip is a short hold. You buy a house below market, fix it up, and sell it within a few months. The profit comes from buying right and keeping every cost on a leash. Below is one full example with round numbers. Chapter3 sells the finished flips it helps buy on the Grand Strand, so this page covers the sale in as much detail as the purchase.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The math</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 1.2rem;line-height:1.1">How a fix and flip works, step by step</h2><ol style="list-style:none;display:grid;gap:.7rem;margin:1.6rem 0;padding:0;max-width:720px"><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">1</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Buy below market.</strong> Work with Chapter3 to find <a href="/invest/foreclosures/" style="color:var(--brass);font-weight:600;text-decoration:none">houses in distress</a> and priced under the market. What you pay sets your profit before any work starts.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">2</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Price the repairs before you offer.</strong> Get a contractor&#x27;s number, not an estimate of your own.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">3</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Monitor holding costs while the work runs.</strong> Every extra month is another month of loan payments, taxes and insurance.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">4</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Work with Chapter3 to sell the finished house.</strong> Price it against what closed nearby, not against what is listed.</p></li><li style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline"><span style="font-family:var(--serif);color:var(--brass);font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:600;min-width:1.8rem">5</span><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin:0"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Pay the tax.</strong> A flip is inventory, not investment property, so it does not qualify for a 1031 exchange.</p></li></ol><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px">Every flip starts with the ARV, what the house will be worth once it is fixed up. Take that number. Subtract everything you spend. What is left is your profit.</p><div style="background:var(--navy);border-radius:12px;padding:1.5rem 1.6rem;margin:1.6rem 0;max-width:600px"><p style="font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass-2);margin-bottom:.9rem">Run your own deal</p><div style="display:grid;gap:.75rem"><label style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:1rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.9);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.93rem">What it sells for fixed up<span style="white-space:nowrap;color:rgba(244,239,232,.55)">$ <input id="flipArv" type="number" min="0" step="1000" value="300000" oninput="c3Flip()" aria-label="What it sells for fixed up in dollars" style="width:132px;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.34);border-radius:6px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.95rem;padding:.42rem .55rem;text-align:right"></span></label><label style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:1rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.9);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.93rem">What you pay<span style="white-space:nowrap;color:rgba(244,239,232,.55)">$ <input id="flipPaid" type="number" min="0" step="1000" value="200000" oninput="c3Flip()" aria-label="What you pay in dollars" style="width:132px;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.34);border-radius:6px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.95rem;padding:.42rem .55rem;text-align:right"></span></label><label style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:1rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.9);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.93rem">Rehab<span style="white-space:nowrap;color:rgba(244,239,232,.55)">$ <input id="flipRehab" type="number" min="0" step="1000" value="45000" oninput="c3Flip()" aria-label="Rehab in dollars" style="width:132px;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.34);border-radius:6px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.95rem;padding:.42rem .55rem;text-align:right"></span></label><label style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:1rem;color:rgba(244,239,232,.9);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.93rem">Holding and selling costs<span style="white-space:nowrap;color:rgba(244,239,232,.55)">$ <input id="flipCosts" type="number" min="0" step="1000" value="30000" oninput="c3Flip()" aria-label="Holding and selling costs in dollars" style="width:132px;background:rgba(244,239,232,.12);border:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.34);border-radius:6px;color:#f4efe8;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.95rem;padding:.42rem .55rem;text-align:right"></span></label></div><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline;border-top:1px solid rgba(244,239,232,.22);margin-top:1.15rem;padding-top:1rem;font-family:var(--sans);color:rgba(244,239,232,.9)"><span>Your profit</span><strong id="flipProfit" style="color:var(--brass-2);font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;line-height:1">$25,000</strong></div><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;align-items:baseline;margin-top:.5rem;font-family:var(--sans);color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);font-size:.9rem"><span>Purchase plus rehab, as a share of the fixed-up value</span><strong id="flipRatio" style="color:var(--ivory)">82%</strong></div><p id="flipVerdict" style="font-family:var(--sans);color:rgba(244,239,232,.72);line-height:1.6;margin:.7rem 0 0;font-size:.92rem">Above the 70 to 75 percent most flippers aim for, so this deal leaves little room for the rehab to run over.</p></div><script>
