-## The four costs fix and flippers need to budget for
-Purchase price and rehab are the obvious numbers. Four more decide whether the margin survives, and every one of them grows the longer you own the house. Budget all four before you make the offer.
+## Do fix and flips make money in Myrtle Beach?
+Most resell for more than the earlier deed price. We read every deed Horry County recorded for two years. Quick resales, a home sold again within 12 months of its last sale, were about 3 of every 100 home sales not made by a builder. The chart gives the middle gain: half gained more, half less.
+Middle gain on a home resold within 12 months, Horry County Who resold it, how many middle gain
 
-### Permits
-In Horry County a permit is required to replace a roof, move walls, or change electrical, plumbing or mechanical systems. Finish work like paint and flooring generally needs none. Unpermitted work brings stop-work orders and fines, and it resurfaces at resale when the buyer's lender asks. Your contractor pulls the permits. Confirm with your contractor that every permit has been applied for and issued.
+Resold by a company · about 140 resales $75,000
+Every quick resale · 344 resales $38,000
+Resold by a person · about 200 resales $15,000
 
-### The loan
-A flip loan charges interest every month you hold the house, and the rate is higher than a normal mortgage. That cost is the reason a project that slips two months can lose the profit it was priced to make. Borrow for the timeline you can hold to, not the one that looks best in the projection.
+The gain between the two deed prices, before repairs, loans, taxes, insurance and both closings. Resales recorded in the 12 months to September 2026. The count is a floor: some sales that may have been a lot that became a new house were left out.
+The company figure is the closer guide to an investor's flip. Resales by a person hold most of the losses: about 55 of the 66 homes that sold for less than the earlier deed price. Houses also gained more than condos, a middle of about $56,000 against about $17,000.
 
-### Holding costs
-Property tax, insurance and utilities keep billing the whole time you own the house. An investment property is taxed at the 6 percent assessment ratio instead of the 4 percent an owner-occupied home gets, so the tax bill is several times what the seller was paying. Our agents run that number on the actual address before you offer.
+## Where on the Grand Strand do flips happen?
+The biggest gains on houses were in Conway, Carolina Forest and Little River. Myrtle Beach had the most quick resales, but most were condos, and the middle one gained about $22,000. No single neighborhood had more than three house resales: the flips are spread across many streets. The deal finder looks at every home for sale for that reason.
+Each number marks where an area's quick resales were, in the order of the chart below. The areas are ZIP codes. Another 13 resales around Loris, Aynor and Green Sea were too few to show. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.
+Middle gain on a home resold within 12 months, by area Area, resales, what sold and middle price paid middle gain
 
-### Closing costs
-You pay a set of fees when you buy and again when you sell, including South Carolina deed stamps of $1.85 per $500 of price on the sale. Attorney fees, title work and recording sit inside the same line. In the example above, holding and selling costs together take $30,000, more than half the rehab budget.
